## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-tenant governance, external collaboration, and how to enforce least privilege with scalable delegation. It also probes how to combine Lighthouse, B2B, PIM, CA, and auditing for a measurable, auditable workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Azure Lighthouse delegation model across tenants
- B2B collaboration and identity management
- Granular RBAC scoping (subscription, resource group, resource)
- Time-bound access with PIM or entitlement packages
- Conditional Access and MFA enforcement
- Auditing, monitoring, and threat detection (Azure Activity Logs, Sentinel)
- Sandbox testing and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: establish Lighthouse delegation and B2B invite flow
async function setupCrossTenantAccess() {
  // 1) create Lighthouse offer in customer tenant
  // 2) MSP accepts and deploys delegated resource access
  // 3) invite partner as B2B guest and assign appropriate roles
  // 4) configure PIM for time-bound activation and MFA
  // 5) enable auditing and sandbox validation
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback path to ensure no orphaned permissions remain?
- Which logs and alerts would you surface to security teams during the window?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of Azure AD B2B, group licensing, Conditional Access, and governance with Access Reviews. It also checks how candidates validate access during and after a time window.

## Key Concepts
- Azure AD B2B guest onboarding
- Group-based licensing
- Conditional Access MFA for guests
- Access Reviews and auto‑revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Graph API (pseudocode) invites a guest and adds to a guest group
async function inviteGuest(email) {
  await graphClient.api('/invitations').post({ invitedUserEmailAddress: email, inviteRedirectUrl: 'https://portal' });
  // add to guests group
  await graphClient.api(`/groups/{guestGroupId}/members/$ref`).post({ "@odata.id": `https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/users/${guestId}` });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle license revocation if a guest leaves early?
- How would you monitor for guests with elevated access beyond 14 days?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical mastery of Azure AD risk-based access controls at scale, including how to design policies, test them safely, and rollback without service disruption.

## Key Concepts

- Identity Protection risk scoring
- Conditional Access policies
- MFA and device compliance
- Session controls and continuous access evaluation
- SIEM integration and audit trails
- Safe rollback and access-review processes

## Code Example

```json
{
  "conditionalAccessPolicy": {
    "displayName": "Risk-based admin access",
    "conditions": {
      "users": { "include": ["admin@contoso.com"] },
      "signInRiskLevels": ["high","medium"],
      "platforms": { "include": ["All"] }
    },
    "grantControls": {
      "builtInControls": ["mfa","deviceCompliance"],
      "sessionControls": ["requireUserConsent","limitSessionDuration"]
    },
    "applications": ["https://portal.contoso.com/admin"]
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate these policies in a sandbox before production?
- How would you measure impact on admin productivity and detect policy drift?
